  "description": "Original study: Forsythe, R., Horowitz, J. L., Savin, N. E., & Sefton, M. (1994). Fairness in simple bargaining experiments. Games and Economic Behavior, 6(3), 347-369. Anonymous pairs: one person decided how to split a sum of money ($5 or $10) with the other, who had no say. Comparing these dictator games with ultimatum games separated fairness from fear of rejection. Dictator games appear in 58 of the 500 studies in our survey. This template has one sender and one receiver, and the two pie sizes as two conditions; the sender may send any amount from 0 to the pie. Participants are simulated: each is a Model participant, using the free test model until you choose a model, so the first runs only check the design; with the test model every participant takes the sample answer.",
